      "why": "The spec requires throughput >= 32 Msps and a p99 batch latency <= 0.44 us for a burst of 32 requests. Only the fully pipelined architectures (1 result/cycle) can sustain 32 Msps while keeping the batch latency tight (N+2 cycles). At 32 Msps, the clock must be >= 32 MHz. A batch of 32 takes 32 cycles to drain. For 32 cycles to fit in 0.44 us, Fmax must be >= 32/0.44 = 72.7 MHz. Pipelined CORDICs with N=12..18 and W=14..18 typically achieve 100-200+ MHz on Artix-7, comfortably meeting the latency and throughput constraints. We search W=14..18 and N=12..18 to find the minimum area design that meets max_abs_err <= 2^-12 (0.000244). Lower W and N reduce area but risk missing the accuracy constraint; the search will map this trade-off."
    }
